- update #stats with `lightCount: 3\nexposure: 1.00` etc.

Light shader with uniforms: uLightPos[3], uLightColor[3], uLightIntensity[3]? Simpler: uniform vec3 uLightPos[3]; uniform vec3 uLightColor[3]; uniform float uIntensity; uniform float uExposure; uniform vec3 uCamPos; uniform sampler2D uAlbedo, uNormal; uniform float uShininess.

Also need world position for lighting! G-buffer has albedo + normal only per requirement "at least albedo + normal". But lighting needs world position. Options: reconstruct from depth, or add a third attachment for position. Requirement says "at least albedo + normal", so I can add position attachment too. Simplest: add third color attachment for world position. I'll do albedo, normal, position (3 attachments) — still satisfies "at least".

Actually I could reconstruct position from depth with inverse VP — more complex. Add position attachment. But gbuffer.frag writes location 0 and 1 only. I can edit gbuffer.frag to add position output — allowed, shaders are mine to complete. I'll add `layout(location=2) out vec4 oPos;`.

Renderer needs to handle resize? Canvas fixed 640x480. Fine.

MRT requires WebGL2 drawBuffers — supported natively.

Write files now. Use apply_patch or heredoc. I'll use apply_patch for each file.

Let me write the light.frag:

```glsl
#version 300 es
precision highp float;
in vec2 vUv;
uniform sampler2D uAlbedo;
uniform sampler2D uNormal;
uniform sampler2D uPosition;
uniform vec3 uCamPos;
uniform vec3 uLightPos[3];
uniform vec3 uLightColor[3];
uniform float uIntensity;
uniform float uExposure;
uniform float uShininess;
out vec4 fragColor;

float attenuation(float d){ return 1.0/(1.0+0.7*d+1.8*d*d); }
void main(){
  vec3 albedo = texture(uAlbedo, vUv).rgb;
  vec3 N = normalize(texture(uNormal, vUv).rgb);
  vec3 P = texture(uPosition, vUv).rgb;
  vec3 V = normalize(uCamPos - P);
  vec3 color = albedo * 0.05;
  for(int i=0;i<3;i++){
    vec3 L = uLightPos[i]-P;
    float dist = length(L);
    L /= dist;
    float att = attenuation(dist);
    float nDotL = max(dot(N,L),0.0);
    vec3 H = normalize(L+V);
    float spec = pow(max(dot(N,H),0.0), uShininess);
    vec3 radiance = uLightColor[i]*uIntensity*att;
    color += (albedo*nDotL + vec3(spec))*radiance;
  }
  color = vec3(1.0)-exp(-color*uExposure);
  fragColor = vec4(color,1.0);
}
```

Wait — background pixels: normal attachment cleared to (0,0,0,0), position (0,0,0). normalize(vec3(0)) is undefined. Clear normal to (0,0,1,0)? Then background gets lit weirdly. Better: use alpha of normal attachment as mask: if alpha < 0.5 → background, output ambient*albedo (albedo cleared to black → black). Set oNormal = vec4(N, 1.0). In light pass: `vec4 nrm = texture(uNormal,vUv); if(nrm.a < 0.5){ fragColor = vec4(vec3(0.0),1.0); return; }` or just multiply. I'll do mask.

